cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pxr-effector-uncoupling: cell-type-resolved coupling of PXR (NR1I2) target genes"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shenoy
    given-names: Amit
    email: shenoy.am@husky.neu.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/xX-its-amit-Xx/pxr-effector-uncoupling"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible analysis identifying hepatocyte-selective coupling of canonical
  PXR (NR1I2) target genes across ten human cell types using 446,672 single cells
  from CELLxGENE Census v2025-01-30. Uses metacell-aggregated Spearman correlations,
  500-resample percentile bootstrap CIs, a metacell-label permutation null with
  BH-FDR control, a 17-combination parameter sweep, a matched 20-gene negative-
  control set, and four external validation layers (GTEx v8 bulk RNA-seq;
  GSE139896 direct rifamycin perturbation in primary hepatocytes; LINCS L1000
  rifampicin signatures across 18 cell lines; Open Targets disease associations).
  Nominates CYP2C8, CYP2C9, CYP3A5 and ABCC2 as direct PXR-responsive hepatocyte-
  selective pharmacodynamic readouts, with SLCO1B1 and CPT1A as hepatocyte-coupled
  but indirectly regulated.
keywords:
  - PXR
  - NR1I2
  - single-cell
  - CELLxGENE
  - pharmacology
  - drug-drug interactions
  - hepatocyte
